#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0397 expect=noViolation domain=FX
#note "The OTHER half of the disjunctive exemption (sheet issue #128, M3-D25, Fix #310): the test was not done (FXSTAT = \"NOT DONE\"), so FXRESCAT is not demanded even though FXSTRESC is not UNREMARKABLE. This arm was already silent under the shipped OR form for the wrong reason - both disjuncts have to hold for the OR to be false - and it is silent under the conjunction because the second conjunct is false. Pinned so the move is bracketed on both exemption halves, not just on the one the sheet issue leads with."
#library standard=sendig-dart version=1-2
dataset FX class=FINDINGS label="Fetal Pathology Findings"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col FXSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col FXTESTCD type=Char label="Fetal Pathology Test Short Name"
col FXSTRESC type=Char label="Character Result/Finding in Std Format"
col FXSTAT   type=Char label="Completion Status"
col FXRESCAT type=Char label="Result Category"
---
S1 | FX | 001 | 1 | FPEXAM |  | NOT DONE | 
